        "[Verse]\nMoonlight reflecting on the piano keys\nRustling sounds of the summer breeze\n\n[Chorus]\nWe sing of love, we sing of loss\nNo matter what the final cost\nThis is the jazz that heals the mind\nThe sweetest comfort we can find",
        "[Verse]\nLate night sessions in a basement club\nAway from the city's noisy hub\n\n[Chorus]\nEvery note telling a story true\nPainting the air in shades of blue\nFeel the groove, let it roll\nDeeply touching the human soul",
        "[Verse]\nAutumn leaves falling on the ground\nNo one else is walking around\n\n[Chorus]\nJust the saxophone playing sad and sweet\nAt the corner where two paths meet\nI close my eyes and let it flow\nTo the place where memories go",
